  "captured_at": "2026-10-14",
  "description": "The TCL Roku TV of tcl-roku-tv-32s357-enabled, ECP network access Enabled, on the home screen. PowerOff left it on the network: device-info answered over plain HTTP and over an authenticated ecp-2 session with power-mode Ready, eight seconds and again seventy seconds after the key, and PowerOn brought back PowerOn with no other field changed. Then a channel launch (Backdrops) and what active-app and media-player answered six seconds later, a keyword search, input to the foreground channel and to Play on Roku (15985, not installed on this set), and two routes the set does not have. The search left active-app on the home screen; the set was returned home with the Home key between steps. Unit and network identifiers use the same emulator-owned values as the earlier TCL captures, the Play on Roku media URL names a documentation address instead of the capturing machine, and the ecp-2 challenge is the fixed nonce with its answer recomputed. The channel icon was answered (image/jpeg) but not retained: it is a channel's trademark artwork."
 },
